# EnvironmentFile for the bare-metal h23 dsa110-calib services.
#
# Install to:  ~/.config/dsa110-calib/dsa110-calib.env
# Referenced by all four dsa110-calib-*.service units as
#   EnvironmentFile=-%h/.config/dsa110-calib/dsa110-calib.env
# (the leading "-" makes it optional, so a missing file degrades to the
# inline Environment= defaults in each unit rather than failing the unit).
#
# NOTE: systemd EnvironmentFile is NOT a shell script. No expansion, no
# quoting rules beyond simple KEY=VALUE, no command substitution.

# --- SSH agent for rsync ---------------------------------------------------
# dsacalib.preprocess.rsync_file() shells out as:
#     . ~/.keychain/calibration-sh; rsync -avv <src> <dst>
# On the container that file is a keychain-managed symlink
# (calibration-sh -> calibration23-sh) exporting SSH_AUTH_SOCK/SSH_AGENT_PID.
# h23's equivalent is ~/.keychain/lxd110h23-sh. The runbook creates the
# compatibility symlink  ~/.keychain/calibration-sh -> lxd110h23-sh  so the
# hardcoded path keeps resolving. Setting SSH_AUTH_SOCK here as well makes
# the unit work even if the keychain agent is not running, PROVIDED the key
# used for the corr nodes does not require an interactive passphrase prompt.
#
# Uncomment and point at a live agent socket if you want agent-based auth:
#SSH_AUTH_SOCK=/run/user/1000/keyring/ssh

# Force a predictable ssh identity + non-interactive behaviour for the
# rsync children. BatchMode prevents a wedged service on a host-key prompt.
RSYNC_RSH=ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=10 -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new

# --- Python / CASA ---------------------------------------------------------
PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1
MPLBACKEND=Agg
HOME=/home/ubuntu
